---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_NAME } from '../config/site';
---

<Base title="Privacy Policy" description="How TextKit handles data: the short version is that tool input never leaves your browser." path="/privacy/">
  <div class="prose">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p><em>Plain-English summary first, details after: {SITE_NAME} tools process everything in your browser. The content you type, paste or generate is never uploaded to us or to anyone else.</em></p>

    <h2>Tool input and output</h2>
    <p>
      Every tool on this site runs as JavaScript in your browser tab. Your input is held in
      the page's memory only, is not transmitted over the network, is not written to any
      server or database, and disappears when you close or reload the page. There are no
      accounts, so there are no profiles, passwords or personal records for us to store.
    </p>

    <h2>What a normal website visit involves</h2>
    <p>
      Like any website, loading a page means the hosting provider serves static files to your
      browser and may keep standard, short-lived server logs (such as IP address and browser
      type) for security and reliability. Pages load fonts from Google Fonts, which means
      your browser contacts Google's font servers when a page is first displayed. If
      advertising is enabled on this site in future, advertising partners may use cookies to
      serve and measure ads; this policy will be updated before that happens.
    </p>

    <h2>Cookies</h2>
    <p>
      The tools themselves set no cookies and use no local storage to keep your content.
      Anything you generate — a password, a UUID, a hash — exists only in the page until you
      copy it away.
    </p>

    <h2>Changes</h2>
    <p>
      If this policy changes, the new version will be published on this page with the date of
      the change. The core commitment — tool content stays in your browser — is architectural
      and will not change.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
